    finding: 'Across 144 experimental tests, reflecting on important values, qualities or relationships (self-affirmation) produced small but reliable increases in accepting a health message (34 tests, N = 3,433, d = 0.17), in intentions to change (64 tests, N = 5,564, d = 0.14) and in later behavior (46 tests, N = 2,715, d = 0.32).',
