    finding: 'In four experiments, positive fantasies that idealized a desired future were linked with less energy (systolic blood pressure and self-report) than fantasies that questioned that future, negative fantasies or neutral ones. In one experiment this showed up a week later as less success with everyday challenges; the more pressing the need, the larger the drop in energy.',
