    finding: 'Gallwey teaches quieting the judging, instruction-giving inner voice (Self 1) so that the body can learn (Self 2), by tying attention to a concrete cue; for example saying “bounce” when the ball hits the ground and “hit” when it meets the racket, and observing the result without judging it as good or bad.',
